{"name":"Portofino","hex":"#f4f09b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Portofino","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A coastal town and comune in the Metropolitan City of Genoa, Liguria, Italy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Portofino"}],"entries":[{"title":"Portofino","blocks":[{"text":"Portofino is a comune located in the Metropolitan City of Genoa on the Italian Riviera. The town is clustered around its small harbour, and is known for the colourfully painted buildings that line the shore. Since the late 19th century, Portofino has attracted tourism of the European aristocracy and it is now a resort for the world's jet set."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Portofino%2C_Italy_2025.jpg/330px-Portofino%2C_Italy_2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portofino","wikidata":"Q232782"},{"title":"Portofino (musical)","blocks":[{"text":"Portofino is a musical with a book by Richard Ney, lyrics by Ney and Sheldon Harnick, and music by Louis Bellson and Will Irwin."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portofino_(musical)","wikidata":"Q7232196"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Portofino_Panorama.jpg/500px-Portofino_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Portofino_Panorama.jpg/1280px-Portofino_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Portofino_Panorama.jpg/500px-Portofino_Panorama.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APortofino_Panorama.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/2016_Portofino_-_Cimitero.jpg/500px-2016_Portofino